Snowpipe:
---------
1. create a IAM role allowing the neccessary access to the S3 bucket get the ARN role id configure in integration 
2. create storage integration 
  create or replace storage integration snowpipe_int
  type = external_stage
  storage_provider = S3
  enabled = TRUE
  storage_aws_role_arn = 'arn:aws:iam::307946640967:role/snowflakede'
  storage_allowed_locations = ('s3://snowflakedebucket1/snowpipe/snowpipe_files')
  comment = 'This is for snowpipe';
3. desc storage integration, take the external id paste it in the IAM role external id
4. create stage 
5. create pipe auto ingest = TRUE and desc pipe get the channel notification and go the S3 bucket and create event notification SQS paste the 
channel notification pass. 
6. all set to the data load via snowpipe. 

To check pipe is running or not:
alter pipe pipename refresh; -- it will tell the files uploaded.
-- Validate pipe is actually working
select system$pipe_status('emp_pipe'); -- says the running status of the pipe.

-- Snowpipe error message:
-- This gives the highlevel of failure
select * from table(validate_pipe_load(
pipe_name => 'pipe_name'
start_time => dateadd(hour, -2, current_timestamp()
));

-- To get granualar level mistake and error follow the below steps:
select * from table(information_schema.copy_history(table_name = 'table_name', start_time => dateadd(hour, -2, current_timestamp())));
/ this will provide the reason of the failure


